{"id":"photosynthesis","title":"Biology: photosynthesis","subject":"Biology","label":"JAMB · WAEC","exams":["jamb","waec"],"language":"en","seconds":184,"duration":183.84,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":493,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Puzzle","start":0,"end":18.785},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":18.785,"end":60.045},{"id":"explain2","title":"Two stages","start":60.045,"end":93.135},{"id":"example","title":"Starch test","start":93.135,"end":120.665},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":120.665,"end":130.105},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":130.105,"end":137.615},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Mistakes","start":137.615,"end":158.485},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":158.485,"end":183.84}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":2.27,"text":"I'm Kora. Here's a puzzle.","w":[0.54,0.7,1.58,1.84,1.9]},{"s":0,"a":2.57,"b":7.82,"text":"A plant has no mouth and no stomach, yet it grows and feeds almost every animal on Earth.","w":[2.62,2.72,3.04,3.26,3.46,3.82,3.96,4.16,4.96,5.14,5.26,5.72,5.9,6.26,6.74,7.06,7.48,7.62]},{"s":0,"a":8.12,"b":12.32,"text":"Where does its food come from, and why does it release the oxygen you breathe?","w":[8.16,8.38,8.58,8.74,9.04,9.28,10.02,10.18,10.42,10.6,10.7,11.06,11.26,11.66,11.82]},{"s":0,"a":12.77,"b":18.36,"text":"Think of a danfo bus; it needs fuel. A plant makes its own fuel, using sunlight.","w":[12.78,13.02,13.14,13.22,13.7,14.44,14.54,14.82,15.58,15.68,16.08,16.34,16.56,16.78,17.52,17.8]},{"s":1,"a":19.21,"b":24.62,"text":"Photosynthesis is how green plants make their own food, glucose, from carbon dioxide and water.","w":[19.32,20.22,20.34,20.58,20.9,21.26,21.42,21.6,21.8,22.42,23.08,23.26,23.58,24.16,24.28]},{"s":1,"a":24.92,"b":29.85,"text":"Light energy is trapped by chlorophyll, the green pigment inside chloroplasts.","w":[25.02,25.3,25.66,25.82,26.2,26.38,27.5,27.64,27.98,28.5,28.96]},{"s":1,"a":30.15,"b":32.84,"text":"So the leaf is a food factory powered by sunlight.","w":[30.26,30.42,30.54,30.86,30.98,31.08,31.32,31.78,32.14,32.32]},{"s":1,"a":33.14,"b":40.06,"text":"The word equation is carbon dioxide plus water gives glucose plus oxygen, in the presence of sunlight and chlorophyll.","w":[33.16,33.32,33.6,34.28,34.46,34.84,35.5,35.82,36.18,36.44,37,37.4,38.24,38.32,38.46,38.84,39,39.44,39.56]},{"s":1,"a":40.36,"b":46.98,"text":"The balanced equation is six C O two plus six H two O gives C six H twelve O six plus six O two.","w":[40.36,40.5,40.9,41.36,41.5,42.08,42.34,42.48,42.76,43.06,43.54,43.68,43.94,44.08,44.36,44.62,45.06,45.18,45.6,45.74,46.04,46.3,46.58,46.7]},{"s":1,"a":47.28,"b":51.61,"text":"It happens in the chloroplasts, mostly in the palisade mesophyll cells of the leaf.","w":[47.32,47.44,47.88,47.96,48.06,49.14,49.58,49.66,49.8,50.32,50.8,51.16,51.26,51.36]},{"s":1,"a":51.91,"b":56.62,"text":"Carbon dioxide enters through the stomata. Water comes up from the roots through the xylem.","w":[51.96,52.34,53.08,53.42,53.64,53.74,54.6,54.92,55.2,55.32,55.48,55.6,55.9,56.08,56.2]},{"s":1,"a":56.92,"b":59.62,"text":"The oxygen released comes from the splitting of water.","w":[56.94,57.2,57.68,58.14,58.42,58.6,58.74,59.14,59.24]},{"s":2,"a":60.47,"b":64.59,"text":"There are two stages. The light dependent stage happens in the grana.","w":[60.52,60.72,60.92,61.18,62.22,62.4,62.68,63.2,63.56,63.98,64.06,64.18]},{"s":2,"a":64.89,"b":70.79,"text":"Light energy splits water, called photolysis, and makes A T P and reduced N A D P.","w":[64.98,65.32,65.74,66.1,66.52,66.8,67.96,68.1,68.48,68.62,68.84,69.22,69.34,69.96,70.16,70.3,70.52]},{"s":2,"a":71.09,"b":74.82,"text":"The light independent stage, the Calvin cycle, happens in the stroma.","w":[71.12,71.26,71.62,72.2,72.84,72.98,73.38,73.8,74.2,74.3,74.4]},{"s":2,"a":75.12,"b":77.92,"text":"There, carbon dioxide is reduced to sugar.","w":[75.14,75.94,76.24,76.9,77,77.42,77.56]},{"s":2,"a":78.22,"b":82.99,"text":"Plants need light, chlorophyll, carbon dioxide, water and a suitable temperature.","w":[78.26,78.64,78.88,79.7,80.4,80.72,81.42,81.9,82.02,82.12,82.54]},{"s":2,"a":83.29,"b":87.86,"text":"The limiting factors are light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration and temperature.","w":[83.32,83.44,83.8,84.28,84.44,84.66,85.58,85.9,86.42,87.3,87.42]},{"s":2,"a":88.16,"b":92.71,"text":"If any one of these is in short supply, the rate of photosynthesis slows down.","w":[88.2,88.44,88.68,88.8,88.9,89.18,89.32,89.52,89.78,90.56,90.72,91.02,91.14,92,92.38]},{"s":3,"a":93.56,"b":96.56,"text":"To test a leaf for starch, first boil it in water.","w":[93.56,93.72,94.02,94.1,94.36,94.56,95.28,95.6,95.94,96.08,96.2]},{"s":3,"a":96.86,"b":99.9,"text":"Then decolourise it in ethanol, using a water bath.","w":[96.94,97.24,97.98,98.1,98.32,99,99.24,99.34,99.64]},{"s":3,"a":100.2,"b":105.39,"text":"Ethanol is flammable, so never heat it directly. That is why we use a water bath.","w":[100.28,100.84,101,101.96,102.18,102.46,102.7,102.8,103.78,104,104.12,104.36,104.58,104.76,104.84,105.14]},{"s":3,"a":105.69,"b":109.05,"text":"Rinse the leaf, add iodine solution, and watch.","w":[105.74,106.02,106.14,106.9,107.26,107.74,108.36,108.54]},{"s":3,"a":109.35,"b":113.76,"text":"Blue-black means starch is present. That shows photosynthesis happened.","w":[109.35,110.02,110.39,110.82,111,111.56,111.86,112.23,113.15]},{"s":3,"a":114.06,"b":120.24,"text":"A variegated leaf with green and white parts shows this nicely. Only the green parts turn blue-black.","w":[114.06,114.18,114.85,115.15,115.45,115.82,116.06,116.42,116.79,117.15,117.45,117.94,118.24,118.48,118.85,119.21,119.51]},{"s":4,"a":121.09,"b":121.65,"text":"Quick check.","w":[121.1,121.36]},{"s":4,"a":121.95,"b":126.82,"text":"Where does the oxygen given off in photosynthesis come from, carbon dioxide or water?","w":[122,122.26,122.44,122.68,123.12,123.44,123.62,123.74,124.54,124.76,125.42,125.76,126.38,126.5]},{"s":4,"a":127.27,"b":129.68,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[127.28,127.64,128,128.14,128.42,129.14,129.32]},{"s":5,"a":130.53,"b":132.17,"text":"The oxygen comes from water.","w":[130.54,130.82,131.3,131.62,131.82]},{"s":5,"a":132.47,"b":137.19,"text":"Light energy splits water in the light dependent stage, and the oxygen is released.","w":[132.54,132.92,133.34,133.76,134.18,134.26,134.4,134.62,135.08,135.74,135.86,136.08,136.6,136.72]},{"s":6,"a":138.04,"b":139.23,"text":"Three common mistakes.","w":[138.08,138.36,138.68]},{"s":6,"a":139.53,"b":143.23,"text":"Do not say plants do not respire; they respire all the time.","w":[139.53,139.68,139.9,140.14,140.52,140.68,140.86,141.76,141.96,142.58,142.74,142.86]},{"s":6,"a":143.53,"b":149.31,"text":"Do not say the dark reaction happens only at night; it does not need light, but it can happen in light too.","w":[143.56,143.74,143.98,144.2,144.34,144.6,145.1,145.56,145.8,145.92,146.66,146.76,146.96,147.14,147.38,147.94,148.1,148.16,148.32,148.66,148.76,149]},{"s":6,"a":149.61,"b":152.89,"text":"Never forget chlorophyll and light when you write the equation.","w":[149.74,150.04,150.46,151.08,151.22,151.7,151.84,152,152.22,152.38]},{"s":6,"a":153.19,"b":158.06,"text":"And in the exam, always say the oxygen comes from water, not carbon dioxide.","w":[153.24,153.46,153.6,153.76,154.6,154.98,155.18,155.38,155.8,156.04,156.22,156.94,157.16,157.46]},{"s":7,"a":158.91,"b":164.9,"text":"Recap. Photosynthesis makes glucose from carbon dioxide and water, using light trapped by chlorophyll.","w":[158.96,159.8,160.68,160.98,161.48,161.68,162,162.54,162.64,163.3,163.6,163.9,164.24,164.4]},{"s":7,"a":165.2,"b":169.46,"text":"It happens in the chloroplasts, and the oxygen comes from the splitting of water.","w":[165.26,165.38,165.74,165.82,165.94,167.1,167.22,167.46,167.96,168.26,168.44,168.58,168.96,169.08]},{"s":7,"a":169.76,"b":173.75,"text":"It feeds almost all living things and gives us the oxygen we breathe.","w":[169.84,169.98,170.4,170.88,171.06,171.38,172.06,172.22,172.5,172.64,172.86,173.26,173.4]},{"s":7,"a":174.05,"b":181.75,"text":"Exam tip: for JAMB and WAEC, write the word equation with sunlight and chlorophyll, and remember the starch test steps.","w":[174.16,174.6,175.26,175.46,175.9,176.06,176.96,177.22,177.34,177.66,178.14,178.36,178.9,179.02,179.98,180.12,180.5,180.64,181,181.34]},{"s":7,"a":182.05,"b":183.24,"text":"Keep going with Knowzone.","w":[182.08,182.32,182.58,182.72]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"A puzzle about plants"},{"at":2.47,"kind":"text","text":"Plant has no mouth or stomach, yet grows"},{"at":8.02,"kind":"text","text":"Where does food come from? Why O2?"},{"at":12.67,"kind":"text","text":"Danfo needs fuel; plant makes fuel using sunlight"}]},{"at":18.96,"heading":"Core idea","items":[{"at":19.11,"kind":"term","text":"Photosynthesis","detail":"Green plants make glucose from CO2 and water using light"},{"at":24.82,"kind":"term","text":"Chlorophyll","detail":"Green pigment in chloroplasts that traps light energy"},{"at":30.05,"kind":"text","text":"Leaf = food factory powered by sunlight"},{"at":30.05,"kind":"image","text":"What goes into the leaf, and what comes out","src":"process.webp","credit":"At09kg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":33.04,"kind":"term","text":"Word equation","detail":"carbon dioxide + water → glucose + oxygen (sunlight, chlorophyll)"}]},{"at":40.11,"heading":"Where it happens","items":[{"at":40.26,"kind":"formula","text":"6CO2 + 6H2O → C6H12O6 + 6O2"},{"at":47.18,"kind":"term","text":"Chloroplasts","detail":"Main site; mostly palisade mesophyll cells in leaf"},{"at":51.81,"kind":"text","text":"CO2 enters via stomata; water via xylem"}]},{"at":60.22,"heading":"Two stages","items":[{"at":60.37,"kind":"text","text":"Two stages: light-dependent and light-independent"},{"at":64.79,"kind":"term","text":"Photolysis","detail":"Light splits water; makes ATP and reduced NADP"},{"at":70.99,"kind":"term","text":"Calvin cycle","detail":"Light-independent stage in the stroma"},{"at":75.02,"kind":"text","text":"CO2 reduced to sugar in stroma"}]},{"at":77.97,"heading":"Limiting factors","items":[{"at":78.12,"kind":"text","text":"Needs light, chlorophyll, CO2, water, suitable temp"},{"at":83.19,"kind":"text","text":"Limiting factors: light, CO2 concentration, temperature"},{"at":88.06,"kind":"text","text":"Short supply of any factor slows the rate"}]},{"at":93.31,"heading":"Starch test","items":[{"at":93.46,"kind":"text","text":"1. Boil leaf in water"},{"at":96.76,"kind":"text","text":"2. Decolourise in ethanol using water bath"},{"at":100.1,"kind":"text","text":"Never heat ethanol directly; use water bath"},{"at":105.59,"kind":"text","text":"3. Rinse, add iodine solution"}]},{"at":109.1,"heading":"Starch test result","items":[{"at":109.25,"kind":"text","text":"Blue-black = starch present"}]},{"at":120.67,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":120.67,"kind":"question","text":"Where does the oxygen given off in photosynthesis come from, carbon dioxide or water?"}]},{"at":130.28,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":130.43,"kind":"text","text":"Oxygen comes from water"},{"at":132.37,"kind":"text","text":"Light splits water; O2 is released"}]},{"at":137.79,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":139.43,"kind":"wrong","text":"Plants do not respire"},{"at":143.43,"kind":"wrong","text":"Dark reaction happens only at night"},{"at":149.51,"kind":"wrong","text":"Equation without chlorophyll and light"},{"at":153.09,"kind":"tip","text":"Exam: oxygen comes from water, not carbon dioxide"}]},{"at":158.66,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":158.81,"kind":"text","text":"Photosynthesis makes glucose from CO2 and water"},{"at":165.1,"kind":"text","text":"Chloroplasts; oxygen from splitting water"},{"at":169.66,"kind":"text","text":"Feeds almost all life; gives oxygen we breathe"},{"at":173.95,"kind":"tip","text":"JAMB/WAEC: word equation with sunlight + chlorophyll; learn starch test"},{"at":181.95,"kind":"text","text":"Keep going with Knowzone"}]}],"check":{"at":129.93,"seconds":10,"question":"Where does the oxygen given off in photosynthesis come from, carbon dioxide or water?","answer":"The oxygen comes from water; light splits water in the light-dependent stage."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[{"title":"Photosynthesis en.svg","author":"At09kg, Wattcle, Nefronus At09kg: original Wattcle: vector graphics Nefronus: re","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photosynthesis_en.svg"}],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}